`Tools.ShippingShipsNoOuts.machine_design_noOuts` is the depth SV head with
the `outsCheck` antecedent removed; its conclusion still asks
`shipsHierCheck (childMap D.modules) b = true`. Its uses of that antecedent:

* passed down to `machine_ships_hierC_at` (the hierarchy head), which opens
  it with `shipsHierCheck_sound` for all eight conjuncts;
* in `design_at`, ONLY for `hierBinds b` (`shipsHierCheck_sound … .1.binds`),
  the gate of the derived `outsCheck` (`hoc`).

On this branch the hierarchy head needs no checker
(`Tools.ShippingShipsHierFree.machine_ships_hierC_free`), and `outsCheck`
follows under the statement-kind gate alone
(`Tools.ShippingChecksCoreGate.core_outsCheck_all_gate`). So:

* `machine_ships_hierC_at_free`: `machine_ships_hierC_free` POINTED at a
  given core run `hcore` and post-processing fact `hpost` (no existential),
